1. **KC=512 broke the cache blocking. This is the main cause.** kcb becomes 504, so each B micro-panel is 504×16×4 ≈ 32 KB, which fills L1 by itself. The six unpacked A rows add 6×504×4 ≈ 12 KB of strided lines on top, so B is evicted on every `ir` step. The per-task A block (96×504×4 ≈ 190 KB) also doubles. That block is re-read for every `jp`, so it now competes for L2. Go back to KCMAX≈256–320, as in Attempt 4. Saving two C passes is worth far less than this.

